**Plan: parse the flag in [`src/cli.js`](src/cli.js), print `buildRows()` as JSON.**

One catch. `toTable` drops `owner` and `slow`. So "same data" reads two ways. I would print the full row.

```js
const json = argv.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

`report.js` and `format.js` stay untouched. Usage string gains `[--json]`.

Next: confirm full rows over the four table columns, then I build it.
